# regressor.tkr — the compiler as its own full-stack regressor (0.3.1, regressor-principal
# design doc, C5). `[tests] regression` (teko.tkp) lists this file FIRST.
#
# THERE IS NO INLINE CODE IN THIS FILE ANY MORE (owner ruling: "está proibido inline code em tkr").
# It carried 275 `Given source inline` blocks and 13.956 lines; every snippet is now a `.tks` file on
# disk. The scenarios did not leave the regressor — they left the SOURCE-CARRYING role, and the build
# count left with them:
#
#   * 65 COMPILE-FAIL scenarios -> one namespace each under the two project-regressors that must fail
#     to compile, sharing those projects' single failing builds (24 parse-stage in
#     member_const_visibility_leak_rejected, 37 checker-stage in
#     const_ns_qualified_visibility_rejected, plus 4 checker PRE-WALK stops and 3 F8 target rows that
#     provably cannot share one).
#   * 187 RUNNABLE scenarios -> one MEMBER NAMESPACE each under the five runnable project-regressors,
#     selected by `TEKO_REGR_ENTRY` and running off those projects' SINGLE builds. Each scenario's
#     text moved, unchanged, into its host project's own `.tkr`; only the selector was added.
#   * what REMAINS below: the four declarative R0 scenarios (living documentation — they build
#     nothing), and the scenarios whose BUILD CONFIGURATION is the thing under test (the own backend,
#     a cross target, a post-build object check) or whose statements carry a top-level `return`.
#     Those cannot share a build with anything by construction, so they keep one each and name their
#     source with `Given source = "examples/regressions/cwd_build/cases/<case>.tks"` — the same build
#     count they always had, with the source now a file a human can open, compile by hand and diff.
#
# The root-project guard (`guard_no_project_build_at_root`) still refuses a scenario here with no
# inline/explicit source — every executable scenario below names its `Given source`.
Feature: R0 — the compiler is its own full-stack regressor (exe native, declarative).

  # The compiler is a native `binary` artifact, so R0 already IS the regressor of the "exe native"
  # artifact kind AND of the whole LANGUAGE. The curated regressors under examples/regressions cover
  # only what R0 structurally CANNOT exercise (other artifact kinds, targets, FFI) — never language
  # features (those live in the Features below + the checker `#test` suite).

  Scenario: the compiler compiles the whole language
    # verified-by: the seed builds gen1 from the umbrella sources (teko . -o bin) — the self-host build.


  Scenario: the compiler passes its own gate
    # verified-by: teko test . exits 0 (600+ checker/build #tests + the D4 coverage floors).


  Scenario: the compiler reaches a byte-identical fixpoint
    # verified-by: gen1 == gen2 byte-identical (the seed-compiled and self-compiled compilers agree),
    # NEVER gen3 — the two-generation fixpoint is the release invariant.


  Scenario: the emitted code agrees across backends
    # verified-by: own==C (F5 backend Examples below) and own==wasm (F5 target-routed scenarios) —
    # the native backend's output matches the C emitter and the wasm target on the shared corpus.

# F3 — the NULL-UNION matrix (regressor-principal-0.3.1.md §3.1). Every shape × operation ×
# recursion cell the owner's mandate calls for, EACH a real, runnable regressive — no partial
# pass. Two cells are HONEST GAPS, not silently dropped: a slice whose ELEMENT is itself a
# null-union (`[]T` where `T = X | null`) is REJECTED today (the parser reads `[](` as a FUNCTION
# type; spelled through an alias it reaches codegen's "optional/slice inner type not yet
# supported"), and an `Iface | null` (interface-in-union) construction is a checker-level
# KNOWN-STOP. Both are PINNED as compile-fail rows — the interface one in
# examples/regressions/const_ns_qualified_visibility_rejected, the slice one in
# member_const_visibility_leak_rejected (parse half) and examples/regressions/qualified_optional
# (codegen half) — so the day support lands each pin fails LOUDLY (an XSTOP, mirroring
# `diff_c_own.sh`'s KNOWN_STOP convention), forcing a conscious promotion to a positive scenario.
# FFI `ptr<T> | null`/`uptr | null` (§3.1 "FFI") is NOT authored — no existing in-tree
# `ptr<T>`/`uptr` USAGE pattern to model a snippet against safely within this wave; flagged for the
# architect/owner, not guessed.


